  "notes": "Two dense pattern sheets carried small, tightly-packed per-size premade-elastic-length tables (near the back yoke and back-leg pieces) that were not transcribed as edges since they are construction notes, not piece dimensions. The sleeve piece's top and bottom corner sub-segment values were genuinely illegible (very small overlapping digits, possibly '4.93'/'0.03'-shaped text) and are recorded as null rather than guessed. A small square piece's own label text could not be confidently read (appears to be a pocket-related gusset/facing but the exact Portuguese term was not legible), so it is flagged originalLabelUnclear. Several other small pieces (yoke, front bodice, small pocket piece) were read with moderate confidence from dense, small-font dimension text and should be treated as 'probably right, worth a second look.'"
